<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Gavere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">23 July <a href="/years/1453">1453</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-ghent-1449-1453">Revolt of Ghent (1449–1453)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Gavere was fought on 23 July 1453 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a>, ending the revolt of Ghent against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. The Ghent militia was routed with heavy losses. Under the peace that followed the city had to pay a large fine, lost many of its privileges and submitted to a humiliating ceremony of apology before the duke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-gavere.jpg" alt="Battle of Gavere" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meister der Privilegien von Gent und Flandern · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:15th-century_painters_-_Surrender_of_the_Burghers_of_Ghent_in_1453_-_WGA15789.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
